    ".acm-happyhours.style-2 .hp-brand": {
      "border-bottom-color": "success"
    },
    ".acm-happyhours.style-3 .hp-link a": {
      "background-color": "accent",
      "color": "accent-on"
    },
    ".example-colors .color-brand-primary, .label-primary": {
      "color": "accent-on!"
    },
    ".list-group-item.active .list-group-item-text": {
      "color": "accent-on"
    },
    ".plain-style .box-contact.box-primary h3": {
      "color": "accent-on",
      "border-color": "accent-on"
    },
    ".plain-style .box-contact.box-primary a": {
      "color": "accent-on"
    },
    ".items-row.cols-1 .info-article .article-aside .category-name a": {
      "background-color": "accent",
      "color": "accent-on"
    },
    ".items-row.cols-1 .info-article .article-aside .category-name a:is(:hover, :focus, :active)": {
      "background-color": "accent-hover",
      "color": "accent-on"
    },
    ".btn-inverse": {
      "background-color": "fg",
      "border-color": "fg",
      "color": "bg"
    },
    ".btn-secondary, button.btn:not([class*=btn-])": {
      "background-color": "surface",
      "border-color": "border",
      "color": "fg"
    },
    "a.btn.btn-default.btn-block.btn-lg": {
      "background-color": "surface-warm",
      "border-color": "surface-warm",
      "color": "fg"
    }
  },
  "followNote": "text the template sets white in one rule on an accent fill set in another (the 'Discover our story' box, the tag chips, the menu's active tab, the accent sidebar module's links): under a light accent it stayed white (1.94 under MotherDuck); it takes the accent's own text. The white cards (#ffffff: special offers, the menu panel) follow as surface (last palette), so their text and fill stay a pair. The yellow marker behind the welcome heading (.hero-heading:before, #ffd33d) takes the surface: the heading text follows the system, and light text on the yellow marker would not read 20/10/2026: the menu cards' dashed rule (#999999) takes the border, the slideshow's ground behind its slides the ink, Happy Hours' badge, brand rule and style-3 button the accent pair or the success colour, the contact page's accent box its text, the swatch and label-primary words and list-group-item-text the accent's own text 20/10/2026 (1.0.6, preview probe v10): the colour themes' category chip reads its brand colour as info and its words as info-text (the same colour): it takes the accent pair; Bootstrap 3's .btn-inverse reads the page colour as its fill and takes the text colour instead (the page's inverse); Joomla core's .btn-secondary and bare button.btn, which Bootstrap 3 leaves to the browser's button face (#6b6b6b under a dark system), take the surface and its text; the gallery's full-width View more bar takes the quiet raised surface; the accent contact box's links keep their colour rule, their 40% underline moved to sideRules",
  "measureBlock": ["*opentable.com/*", "*otstatic.com/*"],
  "measureNote": "the home page's reservation form is OpenTable's own widget, loaded by a parser-blocking script (//secure.opentable.com/frontdoor/…): while that host is slow the page stops at that line and a measure sees only the header and the slider (round 1, and 424 s for one load on 11/10/2026). The measuring browser fails it at once; the form paints with OpenTable's own stylesheet, so it would not follow a system anyway",
