  "sideNote": "Bootstrap 3's status components (alerts, panels, labels, the info button), whose literal pale grounds and status words no tokenizing reached (the release maps some of them to meta, muted and bg): they wear the system's status pairs, as JA Social II (the same T3 Bootstrap) does 20/10/2026 (1.0.6, preview probe v10): the table status rows (.success, .info) the release left literal take the status pairs; the accent-filled menu tabs, pills, active list item and the happy-hours links take the system's button corner; the offer list's dotted accent rule and the accent box's link underline are mixes of the accent and its text; the first feature box's heading is capped at 11% of its box (container units), so a wider face at the template's 58px keeps \"EXPERIENCE\" inside it",
  "faceNote": "the template writes its faces by name rather than through a variable: Roboto Mono on the menu, the topbar's opening hours, module titles, tabs, buttons and the copyright; Noticia Text on the menu dishes and the special-offer titles; Teko on prices, badges, the slideshow words and the account legends. Under a system they stayed the template's beside the system's type (FONT-2 on every page, 20/10/2026): selectors.textFace takes the system's body face, selectors.displayFace its display face, the family only. The split buttons (.btn-decor) keep the template's type (buttonNote) 20/10/2026: the split buttons (.btn-decor) take the system's body family as well (FONT-2 on six pages); size, padding and tracking stay the template's",
  "bandsNote": "blocks of the template’s own colour it was missing drafted 14/10/2026 off its home page and the inner pages the sweep measured (scripts/bands.mjs --draft --fills): the visual review saw them keep the template colour, or white words on a ground that took a light accent. 15/10/2026: the accent Categories module (#Mod97, .module-primary.no-padding, on the home page and the blog) kept its links white (the template's rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8) on .t3-module.module-primary a): the page's followRule for them stops at the band's edge and the band repainted only its title, so under a light accent the four category links read 1.23-2.56:1 (Linear, Mailchimp, Spotify, MotherDuck, Moxie, Toggl Track; v9 measure, 12 of 34 home views and 2 of 8 blog views). The band's words now take the module's content and its links (.module-ct, .module-ct a): the words the system sets on the band's ground 20/10/2026 (1.0.5 measured at preview probe v10): the template paints its dark ink #3a352f as a literal on the main menu bar (.t3-mainnav .container, the phone menu .t3-navbar-collapse), the footer and its modules, the sidebar's dark module (.module-dark) and the second feature box (.acm-features.style-1 .features-item.even), with its second accent #ffd33d on the menu's active item and the footer's links and labels: they stayed brown and yellow under every system (ROLE-1 82% on Toggl Track, Mailchimp and Stripe at 390; ACCENT-LEAK and kept text on 24 of 28 pages). #3a352f is too grey for bands.mjs --fills, so the five are fills of kind ink drafted by hand from bands.mjs on the home page and /about-us: their words take the text the system sets on the worn ground, the yellow words its accent, the menu's lines its card step. The fills, not keepScopes: a kept band gives its inside back to the template (the testimonial name chip and the price tags kept #d24a24). The feature key names .col-sm-6 because the special-offer cards (.acm-features.style-2, white) are .features-item.even too. The accent jumbotron of the typography page is a brand fill, as on Purity III, so its Call to Action stands out on it",
  "buttonNote": "the decorated buttons (.btn-decor: About Us, Learn more) are split buttons, a label box with 78px of right padding beside an arrow cell drawn on that padding: the system’s even padding, type and tracking put the label under the arrow cell, cut to ABOU and LEARN (visual review 14/10/2026). They keep the template’s padding, size and type (left out of selectors.button) and still take the system’s colours",
  "literalsNote": "the first happy-hours description (.acm-happyhours.style-1 .hp-desc) keep the template's own #3a352f under every system: dark words with a white text shadow on a light photograph, which no system ground is under (preview probe v10 20/10/2026: the system's text read 1.68:1 on the photo under Moxie)"
}
